          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which class of biomolecules is responsible for both building cell membranes and carrying chemical signals?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Carbohydrates</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Carbohydrates handle energy storage and cell recognition. Lipids are the class that builds membranes and carries signals.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Lipids</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Lipids perform three key roles: building membranes as phospholipids, storing energy, and carrying chemical signals such as steroid hormones.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Proteins</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Proteins serve as enzymes, transporters, and structural scaffolds. While integral proteins sit within membranes, it is lipids that build the membrane structure itself and carry signals.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Nucleic acids</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Nucleic acids carry genetic information — DNA stores it, RNA transfers it. Lipids are the class that builds membranes and carries signals.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct answer is lipids. They are the class that builds membranes, stores energy, and carries signals — a combination no other biomolecule class provides."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. Lipids have a unique triple role — membrane construction, energy storage, and signal transduction — making them central to cellular organisation."
                }
              ],
