          "label": "<p>Which organelle is unique among sub-cellular components in having no surrounding</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which organelle is unique among sub-cellular components in having no surrounding membrane?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Mitochondria</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Mitochondria have a double membrane — an inner membrane folded into cristae and an outer membrane. Ribosomes are the organelle without any membrane.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Lysosomes</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Lysosomes are single-membrane-bound sacs containing digestive enzymes. Ribosomes are the organelle that has no membrane at all.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Peroxisomes</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. Peroxisomes are membrane-bound organelles responsible for oxidative reactions such as fatty acid breakdown. Ribosomes are the only organelle that lacks a membrane.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Ribosomes</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Ribosomes have no membrane at all. They function as free particles in the cytosol or attached to the rough endoplasmic reticulum, directly reading mRNA to manufacture proteins.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The correct answer is ribosomes. Unlike lysosomes, peroxisomes, and mitochondria — all of which are membrane-enclosed — ribosomes have no surrounding membrane at all."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. Ribosomes are the cell's protein factories and stand apart from other organelles by having no surrounding membrane — they exist as free particles or ER-bound complexes."
                }
              ],
